    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_072dc9868af67378b5382024fd999445accd1f5e00248b95053b2424b278b95b",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: the span gives equivalent functional-equation forms for meromorphic zeta and entire xi and defines the real Hardy Z-function with |Z(t)|=|zeta(1/2+it)|. It states a sign-symmetry principle for Z, proves the k=0 odd-moment instance, leaves higher odd moments conjectural, and contrasts this with the mean-one behavior of powers of zeta. Interpretation: xi exposes entireness and reflection, Z removes critical-line phase to expose real oscillation, and zeta retains arithmetic phase and its small bias. Boundary: statistical indistinguishability of Z and -Z is not a theorem in every stated moment case and does not transfer to zeta values.",
