    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_397f54e7a776d79d2d291d9e51a6d38202099843cab843a96e72b3d926d85a06",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The local factorization and zero-moving construction separate normalized shape, set by nearby zeros, from a slowly varying multiplier. On a complementary set of farther zeros, the weighted neighbor-discrepancy sum reconstructs the logarithm of that multiplier; the product expansion supplies the inverse-neighbor weight, while S(t) supplies an averaged signed readout of whether density is rising or falling.",
