    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_78ff3498b9b4a79fffc86630de14e306b45d71d16db4bdafe2e06d60873281c4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Unfolding removes global geometry so that the GUE and CUE kernels share the sine-kernel local law; matching N to log(T/2pi) by zero density then turns Haar characteristic polynomials into a finite-height model for zeta values. The comparison is deliberately only leading-order: prime-dependent lower terms re-enter as stronger long-range rigidity and damped extremes, while the prescribed Haar sampling makes deterministic unitary counterexamples statistically negligible rather than impossible.",
